🧠 Interview Questions
❓ Difference between `count` and `for_each`?

👉
`count` uses numeric indexes
`for_each` uses named keys and is better for unique resources

❓ What is `depends_on`?

👉 Manual dependency definition when Terraform cannot infer it automatically

❓ What is `lifecycle` used for?

👉 To control creation, destruction, and handling of resource changes

❓ Why use `dynamic` blocks?

👉 To avoid repeating nested configuration blocks

❓ What are sensitive variables?

👉 Variables marked to hide secret values from normal output

🔥 Real Interview Scenario
❓ How do you avoid accidental deletion of production resources?

👉
"I use `lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }` for critical resources like production databases."

❓ How do you create multiple similar resources?

👉
"I use `count` for simple repetition and `for_each` when each resource needs a stable identity."

🧠 Best Practices
Prefer `for_each` when names or keys matter
Use `depends_on` only when Terraform cannot infer dependency
Use `lifecycle` carefully for production safety
Use `dynamic` blocks to reduce repetition in modules
Store secrets securely instead of hardcoding them

✅ Quick Summary
`count` -> repeated resources
`for_each` -> keyed resources
`depends_on` -> manual dependency
`lifecycle` -> resource behavior control
`dynamic` -> repeated nested blocks
Sensitive vars -> protect secrets

